#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:32
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:34
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Color Selection module is comprised of 4 sections:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link linkend=\"kcmdisplay-preview\">The color scheme preview</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:39
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<link linkend=\"kcmdisplay-widget-color\">The current <guilabel>Widget "
"Color</guilabel></link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:42
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<link linkend=\"kcmdisplay-color-schemes\">The available Color Schemes</"
"link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link linkend=\"kcmdisplay-contrast\">The contrast slider</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:48
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A <emphasis>Widget</emphasis> is a commonly-used programmer's term for "
"referring to User Interface elements such as buttons, menus, and scroll "
"bars. You can think of them as the fundamental pieces that are assembled to "
"make your application."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid "Preview"
msgstr "Ulhada"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:57
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This section of the dialog demonstrates how a color scheme applies to a "
"sample selection of widgets. It provides you with a <guilabel>preview</"
"guilabel> of your current color choices."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid "A color scheme consists of a set of 18 colors."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:63
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each of the widgets is labeled to help you identify how your changes will "
"impact the color scheme."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid "Widget Color"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The currently selected member of the color scheme is shown in the combo box. "
"This widget color can be changed by clicking on the colored box below the "
"combo box. A color selection dialog will then appear, from which you may "
"select a new color. When you are happy with your color selection, press "
"<guibutton>OK</guibutton> in the color selection dialog. The color will be "
"updated in the Preview Area."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid "You may select any member of the color scheme from the color combination box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Contrast</guilabel> Slider"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Contrast</guilabel> slider allows you to change the contrast "
"between different shadings of the selected colors."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid "The preview area instantly updates to show the effect of your change."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid "Color Scheme"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Various color schemes are supplied with &kde;, and you are free to define "
"your own."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The three major color components of each scheme are shown beside the name in "
"the list. To preview a scheme in the larger preview area, click on its name "
"in the list box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use the &kde;-supplied Color Schemes as a starting point to devise "
"your own Scheme. Click on the <guibutton>Save Scheme...</guibutton> button "
"to store the color scheme under a new name, then modify it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When such a user-created Color Scheme is selected, changes to it (as shown "
"in the Preview) can be saved with the <guibutton>Save Scheme...</guibutton> "
"button; it can also be deleted with the <guibutton>Remove Scheme</guibutton> "
"button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kde;-supplied Schemes themselves cannot be changed or deleted."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use the <guibutton>Import Scheme...</guibutton> button to add new "
"entries to the list. This might be color schemes that you have created on "
"another computer and saved, or color schemes you have downloaded from a "
"website."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can choose if you want &kde; to apply the color scheme even to non-&kde; "
"applications by enabling the <guilabel>Apply colors to non-KDE applications</"
"guilabel>. Not all applications will allow this, but most do."
msgstr ""

